WEBVTT

00:00:02.581 --> 00:00:06.804
One question was left open. Does Telo Ride 1 keep a backend?

00:00:10.324 --> 00:00:15.304
The backend signs riders in, keeps their progress, runs live races and group

00:00:15.304 --> 00:00:20.780
classes, and lists the classes. Telo Ride 1 leaves out all of it but one class.

00:00:23.228 --> 00:00:27.900
The requirements already point one way: static files, your record kept on your

00:00:27.900 --> 00:00:31.255
device, and a ride that finishes without a network.

00:00:36.133 --> 00:00:40.214
So the answer is no. The class ships with the app, and there is nothing to keep

00:00:40.214 --> 00:00:40.927
running.

00:00:49.038 --> 00:00:53.742
The backend goes piece by piece, each with the slice that removes what it served,

00:00:53.742 --> 00:00:56.249
and the build stays green all the way.

00:01:01.942 --> 00:01:06.112
Nothing on screen changes today. The app looks the same at every width.

00:01:12.266 --> 00:01:17.920
Telo Ride 1, from the Telo family, is the focused edition of Telo Ride: one class,

00:01:17.920 --> 00:01:19.116
nothing else.

00:01:19.461 --> 00:01:24.413
It pairs with a smart bike at home over Bluetooth, plays the class video, or draws

00:01:24.413 --> 00:01:29.425
the Ibiza Sunset Strip course to music if the rider chooses it, and sets the bike's

00:01:29.425 --> 00:01:32.926
resistance for every interval while the rider pedals.

00:01:33.272 --> 00:01:37.247
Connect the bike, take the class, see your number, and come back to beat it.
